      "slug": "lesson-69cd1a5df775",
      "topic": "ada nest heartbeat escalation",
      "created": true,
      "content": "<h3>How Ada Nest Heartbeat Escalation Works</h3><p>Each member node sends a heartbeat at a fixed interval. The hub monitors the timestamps of these heartbeats. If a node fails to send <strong>N</strong> consecutive heartbeats, its status becomes <em>stale</em> and then <em>degraded</em>. Only after the degraded period expires without a heartbeat does the hub trigger an escalation (e.g., a page or alert). A single missed heartbeat or a brief network glitch does not cause an escalation.</p>",
      "next_review": "2026-10-31",
      "status": "open"
     }
    ],
    "tool_calls": 2
